---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'

const mail = 'mailto:contact@gamedevjsweekly.com?subject='
---

<Layout title={'Sponsor'} desc={'Sponsor Gamedev.js Weekly, the independent newsletter for web game developers. Reach 8,000+ subscribers every Friday, since 2014.'}>
  <main id=m-s class=l-c>
    <header id=p-h>
      <small>
        Sponsor the newsletter
      </small>
      <h1>Get your product in front of web game developers</h1>
    </header>
    <section>
      <p>
        Gamedev.js Weekly is an independent newsletter covering the tools, tutorials, games and ideas shaping web game development. Every Friday since January 2014, we've shared the best links with a dedicated audience of developers.
      </p>
      <a class=i-b href={mail + 'Gamedev.js%20Weekly%20sponsorship%20inquiry'}>Ask about availability</a>
    </section>
    <section id=m-s-s class=f aria-label='Newsletter at a glance'>
      <div><b>8,000+</b><span>Active subscribers</span></div>
      <div><b>2014</b><span>Published continuously since</span></div>
      <div><b>Every Friday</b><span>One focused issue each week</span></div>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>A focused developer audience</h2>
      <p>
        Our readers are people building games and interactive experiences for the web. They follow JavaScript and HTML5 game technology, engines, tools, tutorials, demos and new releases. The subscriber list has grown organically, and inactive accounts are regularly removed.
      </p>
      <h3>Who you're reaching</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>JavaScript and HTML5 game developers</li>
        <li>Indie game creators and small studios</li>
        <li>Engine, framework and developer-tool users</li>
        <li>People interested in games, web technologies and creative coding</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Newsletter engagement</h3>
      <p>
        Recent historical averages are approximately <strong>25-35% opens</strong> and <strong>6-12% overall newsletter click rates</strong>, measured after publication. These figures describe whole-issue engagement, not guaranteed sponsor performance.
      </p>
      <p>
        Browse the <a href=archive>public archive</a> to see the content and editorial context of a typical issue.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id=packages>
      <h2>Sponsorship options</h2>
      <p>
        Straightforward, relevant sponsorships with clear labelling. A good fit for game engines, web development tools, SDKs, courses, events, platforms, and services for game developers.
      </p>
      <div id=m-s-p>
        <article>
          <small>Standard sponsorship</small>
          <strong>$300 <span>/ issue</span></strong>
          <p>A text-based sponsored entry, presented in the familiar light-blue style used in our newsletter.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Title, short description and destination URL</li>
            <li>Placement in an appropriate editorial section</li>
            <li>Clearly marked as sponsored content</li>
            <li>One Friday newsletter issue</li>
          </ul>
          <a class=i-b href={mail + 'Standard%20sponsorship%20-%20Gamedev.js%20Weekly'}>Enquire about standard</a>
        </article>
        <article class=m-s-f>
          <small>Featured sponsorship</small>
          <strong>$450 <span>/ issue</span></strong>
          <p>Extra visibility for launches and campaigns that need a more prominent position.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Prominent sponsored placement near the beginning</li>
            <li>Title, description, destination URL and optional small logo</li>
            <li>Exclusive commercial sponsorship for that issue</li>
            <li>Clearly marked as sponsored content</li>
          </ul>
          <a class=i-b href={mail + 'Featured%20sponsorship%20-%20Gamedev.js%20Weekly'}>Enquire about featured</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p id=m-s-n>
        <strong>Planning a campaign?</strong> Standard placements are also available for <strong>two issues at $550</strong> or <strong>four issues at $1,000</strong>, subject to availability. Longer campaigns and job listings can be discussed individually.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>What does a sponsor placement look like?</h2>
      <p>
        We keep sponsorships useful and recognizable. Standard advertisements are text-first, with a light blue background so they stand apart from independent editorial recommendations.
      </p>
      <h3>Simple copy requirements</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>A descriptive title (around 80 characters or fewer)</li>
        <li>A short description (ideally up to 160 characters)</li>
        <li>One destination URL</li>
        <li>Optional logo for featured placements</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All material is reviewed for relevance, accuracy and fit. We may suggest edits for clarity and consistency with the newsletter.
      </p>
      <h3>Example</h3>
      <div id=m-s-d aria-label='Example sponsored newsletter entry'>
        <a href=#>Make better web games with Example Toolkit</a>
        <p>A practical toolkit for JavaScript game developers, with reusable components and a simpler workflow for your next browser game.</p>
      </div>
      <p>
        <span class=m-s-h>Illustrative example, not a live advertisement. Final layout follows the newsletter template and may vary slightly.</span>
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol id=m-s-h>
        <li>
          <h3>1. Tell us about your project</h3>
          <p>Send a short introduction, your URL and the issue or timeframe you have in mind.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>2. Confirm your placement</h3>
          <p>We'll check relevance and availability, agree on the format and date, and arrange payment.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>3. Reach our readers</h3>
          <p>Provide the final copy in advance. Your clearly identified placement goes out in the confirmed Friday issue.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>A few useful details</h2>
      <h3>Can I promote an indie game on a smaller budget?</h3>
      <p>
        We also have limited community-sponsored opportunities for independent developers. These are separate from commercial advertising. See the <a href=about#submit>About page</a> for submission details.
      </p>
      <h3>Can I advertise a job opening?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. Relevant openings can be placed in the Jobs section. <a href={mail + 'Job%20listing%20-%20Gamedev.js%20Weekly'}>Get in touch</a> for availability and pricing.
      </p>
      <h3>Is publication guaranteed once I enquire?</h3>
      <p>
        Not until we've confirmed the placement. All advertisements are subject to editorial approval and available space. We don't guarantee a particular number of opens, clicks or conversions.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Interested in sponsoring an issue?</h2>
      <p>
        Tell us what you're promoting and when you'd like it to appear.
      </p>
      <a class=i-b href={mail + 'Gamedev.js%20Weekly%20sponsorship%20inquiry'}>Get in touch</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
